# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MCS 3950 — group project
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Imagery. Large, and its redistribution is restricted — do not commit it.
# Commit code, configuration, and small result artefacts instead.
#
# Note the pattern: `data/*` rather than `data/`. Git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so excluding the directory outright would
# make the two negations below impossible and the folder would not clone at all.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md
*.tif
*.tiff
*.jp2
*.ecw
*.sid
*.img
*.HEIC

# Large rasters anywhere in the tree. If you need to commit a small figure,
# put it in results/ and force-add it:  git add -f results/figure1.png
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
!results/**
!docs/**

# Model weights and checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
*.ckpt
*.onnx
checkpoints/
runs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
*.egg-info/

# Jupyter — strip outputs before committing where you can; a notebook full of
# embedded images makes diffs unreadable and bloats the repository.
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb

# Environment and secrets — never commit these
.env
*.key
*.pem
credentials.json

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
